1
00:00:49,632 --> 00:00:51,301
Viktor! Viktor!

2
00:00:54,429 --> 00:00:58,224
Cute, but we still have a long way to go.

3
00:00:58,308 --> 00:00:59,726
But where are we going?

4
00:01:08,276 --> 00:01:10,445
Forget all those emotions.

5
00:01:10,528 --> 00:01:11,404
It's all nonsense!

6
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:13,323
Whatever kindness they've shown you,

7
00:01:13,406 --> 00:01:16,159
<i>whatever kindness Mikoy and Chiara</i>
<i>have shown you,</i>

8
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:17,494
<i>forget all of it.</i>

9
00:01:17,577 --> 00:01:19,079
What matters most of all

10
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:21,539
is the plan we're all working on.

11
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:23,708
Forget those emotions.

12
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:25,877
They don't matter!

13
00:01:29,130 --> 00:01:31,174
Help me serve the food I brought

14
00:01:31,257 --> 00:01:34,177
so our watch party
will be more fun, right?

15
00:01:34,260 --> 00:01:35,595
Come on!

16
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,060
Wait, you know what?

17
00:01:42,143 --> 00:01:44,562
I just remembered.
I have a gift for Chiara.

18
00:01:44,646 --> 00:01:45,730
Wait here, okay?

19
00:01:47,774 --> 00:01:49,359
- Bro.
- I'll leave this to you, okay?

20
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:51,694
- I'll take care of it.
- Thanks.

21
00:02:11,714 --> 00:02:12,882
<i>Seems like before,</i>

22
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:16,469
<i>I used to joke about</i>
<i>walking you down the aisle.</i>

23
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:19,305
Chiara, I am so sure.

24
00:02:26,771 --> 00:02:29,190
- Are you sure?
- Yes.

25
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,693
Look at my face.

26
00:02:35,697 --> 00:02:36,990
Look at my face.

27
00:02:44,706 --> 00:02:45,915
Ouch!

28
00:02:46,583 --> 00:02:47,417
<i>But now,</i>

29
00:02:49,002 --> 00:02:50,295
<i>it's almost here.</i>

30
00:02:51,713 --> 00:02:53,214
<i>Just a little longer,</i>

31
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:55,049
<i>and it will finally come true.</i>

32
00:02:58,928 --> 00:03:02,348
<i>It's almost like fate was playing a joke</i>
<i>when we first met.</i>

33
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:06,185
<i>But we also proved, beyond a doubt,</i>

34
00:03:06,269 --> 00:03:08,313
<i>that we really are meant for each other.</i>

35
00:03:11,065 --> 00:03:12,191
I'm listening.

36
00:03:17,864 --> 00:03:19,616
<i>Chiara, I love you so much,</i>

37
00:03:19,699 --> 00:03:21,409
<i>so I accept you.</i>

38
00:03:25,413 --> 00:03:29,500
<i>I didn't want you to find out</i>
<i>about this side of me.</i>

39
00:03:30,126 --> 00:03:32,795
<i>I was so scared you'd find out.</i>

40
00:03:34,589 --> 00:03:37,550
I don't feel worthy of being loved.

41
00:03:44,515 --> 00:03:46,017
<i>Chiara, never say that.</i>

42
00:03:46,893 --> 00:03:48,603
<i>We all deserve to love,</i>

43
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:50,188
<i>especially you.</i>

44
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:53,191
<i>But the truth is,</i>
<i>there's only one thing I want.</i>

45
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:55,026
I just want to be with you.

46
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:01,532
<i>I can't wait to spend</i>
<i>the rest of my life with you.</i>

47
00:04:03,284 --> 00:04:07,038
<i>You are truly a blessing in my life.</i>

48
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:12,460
<i>I love you so, so, so much, Chiara.</i>

49
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:18,174
<i>Mikoy.</i>

50
00:04:29,894 --> 00:04:31,771
What could this be?

51
00:04:40,280 --> 00:04:41,572
So cute!

52
00:04:42,198 --> 00:04:44,200
There's a Chiara too!

53
00:04:51,541 --> 00:04:55,128
Sorry, guys,
if I have to be a killjoy, okay?

54
00:04:55,211 --> 00:04:57,839
But we have a schedule
that you need to follow.

55
00:04:58,423 --> 00:04:59,674
So,

56
00:05:01,342 --> 00:05:04,637
It's time to leave our bride

57
00:05:04,721 --> 00:05:06,723
for the finishing touches.

58
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:08,683
So come on, let's go, go, go.

59
00:05:08,766 --> 00:05:10,643
Wait. Wait a second.

60
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:13,271
Chiara, if you need anything,
I'll just be in the next room, okay?

61
00:05:13,354 --> 00:05:15,398
Actually, can I ask you a favor?

62
00:05:15,481 --> 00:05:16,524
Sure. What is it?

63
00:05:16,607 --> 00:05:18,276
My gift for Mikoy.

64
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:20,862
Okay, sure. I'll get it.

65
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:25,992
Don't worry, I'll make sure he gets it.

66
00:05:28,828 --> 00:05:29,954
- See you.
- See you!

67
00:05:30,038 --> 00:05:32,081
- Okay go ahead.
- We have to go.

68
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:32,999
Come on, come on.

69
00:05:35,626 --> 00:05:36,711
No, not like that.

70
00:05:36,794 --> 00:05:37,920
Where's the one doing the retouch?

71
00:05:40,798 --> 00:05:42,967
I want it perfect. You have to look good.

72
00:05:43,051 --> 00:05:44,594
Beautiful, flawless.

73
00:05:44,677 --> 00:05:45,928
Okay, there. That's it.

74
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:49,140
Okay.

75
00:05:49,724 --> 00:05:52,226
On the count of three,
come closer slowly and smile, okay?

76
00:05:56,606 --> 00:05:58,900
Sir, not much.

77
00:05:58,983 --> 00:05:59,817
Okay.

78
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:02,403
Okay, one, two, three, look at me.

79
00:06:04,280 --> 00:06:05,531
- Mikoy, Mikoy.
- A little more.

80
00:06:05,615 --> 00:06:08,409
He said don't show your teeth.

81
00:06:08,493 --> 00:06:09,452
Just like that.

82
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,497
- There.
- Okay, okay.

83
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:13,956
- My goodness.
- There.

84
00:06:14,040 --> 00:06:15,083
How do I do that?

85
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:18,377
Like that.

86
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:20,922
Like that, right?

87
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:21,839
But, son,

88
00:06:21,923 --> 00:06:23,341
that's really part of it, okay?

89
00:06:23,424 --> 00:06:24,550
You have to own it.

90
00:06:24,634 --> 00:06:27,845
You have to feel like you're GGSS.

91
00:06:27,929 --> 00:06:29,388
- There!
- GGSS!

92
00:06:29,472 --> 00:06:31,724
- Okay, okay, okay.
- It's easy. Try it.

93
00:06:31,808 --> 00:06:33,142
Okay, try.

94
00:06:38,898 --> 00:06:40,483
Still not it.

95
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:43,069
- One more, one more.
- One more.

96
00:06:43,152 --> 00:06:45,822
- How are you supposed to smile, sir?
- Relax.

97
00:06:45,905 --> 00:06:47,406
Just relax.

98
00:06:48,407 --> 00:06:50,159
- Let's just relax.
- Okay.

99
00:06:51,035 --> 00:06:54,163
Mikoy, just relax.

100
00:06:54,247 --> 00:06:55,998
If you don't overthink your smile,

101
00:06:56,082 --> 00:06:58,334
your natural charm
will come out even more.

102
00:06:59,627 --> 00:07:00,545
Right.

103
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:03,131
Okay, okay, sure.

104
00:07:03,214 --> 00:07:04,757
- Again.
- Okay.

105
00:07:04,841 --> 00:07:05,758
Look into the distance.

106
00:07:05,842 --> 00:07:08,261
Look at me, one, two, three.

107
00:07:13,599 --> 00:07:15,852
- There you go!
- You got it!

108
00:07:16,644 --> 00:07:18,479
You're really good, Agent Alex!

109
00:07:18,980 --> 00:07:20,606
Agent is all we need.

110
00:07:20,690 --> 00:07:23,109
Oh, and Chiara
asked me to give this to you.

111
00:07:23,192 --> 00:07:24,193
Her gift.

112
00:08:24,170 --> 00:08:29,926
<i>That you're the kind of person</i>
<i>I could never get tired of talking to,</i>

113
00:08:30,009 --> 00:08:32,595
<i>teasing, and drinking with.</i>

114
00:09:07,964 --> 00:09:09,215
Ben!

115
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:11,968
Looks like we're short on soft drinks.

116
00:09:12,552 --> 00:09:14,178
Go get some from the pantry, okay?

117
00:09:14,262 --> 00:09:15,346
Right.

118
00:09:15,429 --> 00:09:16,472
Yes, General.

119
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:27,483
I went over your profiling report
on the immediate community in Albay.

120
00:09:28,776 --> 00:09:31,070
It seems a little too ordinary.

121
00:09:31,153 --> 00:09:32,238
Nothing stands out.

122
00:09:33,197 --> 00:09:34,532
That's the tricky part.

123
00:09:35,825 --> 00:09:40,288
Sometimes something ordinary can also mean

124
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:43,374
there's something too good to be true.

125
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:47,253
Someone stood out to me.

126
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:48,713
Really, sir?

127
00:09:48,796 --> 00:09:49,672
Who?

128
00:09:50,506 --> 00:09:52,049
That vlogger.

129
00:09:52,883 --> 00:09:54,343
Rahmboy.

130
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:55,886
Rahmboy.

131
00:09:56,762 --> 00:09:57,805
That's the one.

132
00:10:04,312 --> 00:10:05,229
Ben!

133
00:10:06,856 --> 00:10:08,065
Where is he?

134
00:10:16,365 --> 00:10:17,658
<i>Be careful.</i>

135
00:10:17,742 --> 00:10:19,410
<i>Especially around Agent Alex.</i>

136
00:10:19,910 --> 00:10:22,997
<i>Nothing changes in the plan.</i>
<i>We're going through with it.</i>

137
00:10:50,816 --> 00:10:51,776
Sofie!

138
00:10:54,070 --> 00:10:55,821
There you go, there you go.

139
00:10:55,905 --> 00:10:57,406
Just a second.

140
00:10:58,282 --> 00:10:59,367
Hey!

141
00:10:59,450 --> 00:11:00,701
- Oh, geez.
- Wait, wait.

142
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:02,578
I know you’re not talking to anyone.

143
00:11:09,293 --> 00:11:10,211
Sofie.

144
00:11:13,881 --> 00:11:15,007
Sofie.

145
00:11:15,091 --> 00:11:16,592
He passed out!

146
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:57,508
Let me just confirm something.

147
00:11:57,591 --> 00:11:59,677
The one I sent you,
that's Cocoy's car, right?

148
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:01,512
Yes, it is.

149
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:02,805
It's his,

150
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:05,182
and it's confirmed that Cocoy isn't here.

151
00:12:05,975 --> 00:12:07,476
And Carlota isn't here either.

152
00:12:08,102 --> 00:12:11,230
That's why they weren't responding
in the group chat earlier.

153
00:12:11,313 --> 00:12:13,899
I thought they were with the remote team
this whole time,

154
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:15,484
but it turns out they're with Team Albay.

155
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:19,363
- What? They're both here?
- <i>Yes.</i>

156
00:12:20,865 --> 00:12:22,867
Wait, guys, we have an update.

157
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,869
Someone I know said

158
00:12:24,952 --> 00:12:28,080
someone broke Viktor out
last night, there.

159
00:12:32,960 --> 00:12:34,795
Looks like she escaped too.

160
00:12:34,879 --> 00:12:36,964
What? What's happening?

161
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:38,424
And who would break them out?

162
00:12:38,507 --> 00:12:40,134
Unless the Valtrovis are here.

163
00:12:50,311 --> 00:12:51,896
Angelito?

164
00:12:53,981 --> 00:12:55,316
Angelito.

165
00:12:57,693 --> 00:12:58,527
You're too slow.

166
00:12:58,611 --> 00:12:59,612
I'll do mouth-to-mouth. I'll do it.

167
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:01,030
Hold that.

168
00:13:01,113 --> 00:13:02,323
Hold this. Hurry up.

169
00:13:02,406 --> 00:13:04,533
Move aside. Go on, do it. Go!

170
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:06,577
Hey, what do you mean, you?

171
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:08,496
I'm doing the mouth-to-mouth!
Get out of there!

172
00:13:08,579 --> 00:13:10,372
- All of you, move!
- Come on.

173
00:13:11,081 --> 00:13:12,291
Angelito.

174
00:13:13,292 --> 00:13:14,460
You're taking too long.

175
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:16,003
Hurry! Come on, hurry!

176
00:13:16,086 --> 00:13:17,171
- You’re too slow!
- So slow.

177
00:13:17,254 --> 00:13:19,173
Wait, wait, wait!

178
00:13:19,673 --> 00:13:20,591
It's my first time!

179
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:39,902
Just leave them.

180
00:13:40,486 --> 00:13:41,946
They'll come back.

181
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,406
Did I hear that right?

182
00:13:46,617 --> 00:13:49,078
General Norberto said so.

183
00:13:52,248 --> 00:13:56,252
I understand if you're surprised.

184
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:59,505
<i>It's more than just a surprise, sir.</i>

185
00:14:00,172 --> 00:14:01,882
We're completely shook!

186
00:14:02,800 --> 00:14:03,634
Sir,

187
00:14:04,718 --> 00:14:07,388
it's a good thing
the higher-ups agreed to this,

188
00:14:07,471 --> 00:14:10,933
because they know Viktor and his people
are a high-profile case.

189
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:25,698
I just thought that since
Chiara killed La Morte Bianca,

190
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:29,118
and we secured the bomb,

191
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:39,169
for the two of them.

192
00:14:39,795 --> 00:14:40,963
I agree, sir.

193
00:14:41,714 --> 00:14:43,883
I'm sure Chiara must
be very happy right now.

194
00:14:45,342 --> 00:14:48,512
Sir, didn't that favor you asked for
come with a price, too?

195
00:14:48,596 --> 00:14:49,805
That's right, sir.

196
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:52,391
The higher-ups might come after you.

197
00:15:04,778 --> 00:15:09,491
His sudden transfer of Viktor and Brusko
to a highly secured prison,

198
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:12,411
on top of the string of violence
that happened inside.

199
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:14,622
<i>With what he did,</i>

200
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:18,125
<i>it's very obvious</i>
<i>that he has it out for Viktor.</i>

201
00:15:19,084 --> 00:15:21,629
Exactly. You're absolutely right, sir.

202
00:15:22,671 --> 00:15:25,841
But knowing Senator Quintin's connections,

203
00:15:27,009 --> 00:15:29,386
sooner or later,
you might get a memo about this.

204
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:42,274
<i>For now, just think of me as a boss</i>
<i>who isn't a killjoy.</i>

205
00:15:42,358 --> 00:15:45,694
And since I rarely ask
the higher-ups for a favor,

206
00:15:53,744 --> 00:15:56,205
- One for the books, that's for sure!
- Yes.

207
00:16:03,045 --> 00:16:04,380
More pizza!

208
00:16:23,190 --> 00:16:24,858
Hey, Sofie!

209
00:16:27,945 --> 00:16:29,738
Don't avoid me now.

210
00:16:30,447 --> 00:16:31,532
Me?

211
00:16:31,615 --> 00:16:33,659
Weren't you the one
avoiding me all this time?

212
00:16:34,243 --> 00:16:36,203
How does it feel
to be the one being avoided?

213
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:38,205
Awkward, isn't it?

214
00:16:39,039 --> 00:16:41,458
How does it feel to be
on the receiving end?

215
00:16:50,509 --> 00:16:53,429
Just because we got drunk the other day

216
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:56,890
doesn't mean any of that wasn't real.

217
00:17:03,147 --> 00:17:04,023
Because

218
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:06,275
the truth is,

219
00:17:09,445 --> 00:17:10,404
I like you.

220
00:17:26,420 --> 00:17:27,713
That's your answer? Okay?

221
00:17:28,964 --> 00:17:30,215
You're so nonchalant.

222
00:17:36,138 --> 00:17:38,474
Or we could go with "bebu."

223
00:17:40,017 --> 00:17:41,810
Then,

224
00:17:42,394 --> 00:17:43,228
love.

225
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:18,639
The bride isn't done yet!

226
00:18:18,722 --> 00:18:20,724
She'll come out according to our schedule.

227
00:18:20,808 --> 00:18:21,975
Keep going.

228
00:18:23,602 --> 00:18:25,437
You're so persistent!

229
00:18:25,521 --> 00:18:27,147
She's really not done yet!

230
00:18:36,323 --> 00:18:38,909
I'm sorry, no offense, but it's important.

231
00:18:38,992 --> 00:18:41,370
There's a surprise for the bride.

232
00:19:23,704 --> 00:19:25,247
Senator, there's bad news.

233
00:19:26,165 --> 00:19:26,999
What is it?

234
00:19:27,624 --> 00:19:30,460
Viktor escaped, along with Donabel.

235
00:19:35,090 --> 00:19:36,550
How did that happen?

236
00:19:36,633 --> 00:19:37,509
When?

237
00:19:38,760 --> 00:19:39,803
Just last night.

238
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:42,639
It was sudden.

239
00:19:42,723 --> 00:19:45,100
Looks like someone
up top gave the go-ahead.

240
00:19:52,649 --> 00:19:55,569
Someone had the nerve to bypass me?

241
00:19:56,153 --> 00:19:58,906
And who are these annoying people?

242
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:10,083
She's so beautiful, Viktor. Look at her.

243
00:20:15,756 --> 00:20:18,217
That's nothing. Look, I have another one.

244
00:20:41,823 --> 00:20:42,908
My child.

245
00:20:47,412 --> 00:20:50,707
Sorry, okay? This is all we could manage.

246
00:20:57,339 --> 00:20:59,424
Here's another one. Look.

247
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:04,221
Sorry, but I was the one
who picked all of these.

248
00:21:04,304 --> 00:21:05,222
Chiara.

249
00:21:11,853 --> 00:21:13,647
It all happened so suddenly, right?

250
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:15,816
We didn't expect we'd be able to make it.

251
00:21:15,899 --> 00:21:17,943
- Exactly.
- Your father and I are so happy.

252
00:21:28,829 --> 00:21:30,122
What an irony.

253
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:35,419
Back when we were living the good life,

254
00:21:36,461 --> 00:21:40,340
we could easily
get you anything you wanted.

255
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:42,968
Everything was within reach.

256
00:21:50,183 --> 00:21:51,268
Yes, that's true.

257
00:21:51,351 --> 00:21:52,436
Remember, honey?

258
00:21:52,519 --> 00:21:53,729
Oh, my gosh.

259
00:21:54,313 --> 00:21:55,772
We used to shop like crazy!

260
00:21:56,398 --> 00:21:58,775
Right? You know that.

261
00:21:58,859 --> 00:22:01,069
You always knew how much our bill was.

262
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,612
We really shopped like crazy.

263
00:22:02,696 --> 00:22:05,115
The shopping couldn't keep up with us.

264
00:22:07,868 --> 00:22:09,745
I remember this one time,

265
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:15,542
we bought so much stuff, and then
we just gave it all to the saleslady.

266
00:22:15,625 --> 00:22:17,461
And they were so shocked.

267
00:22:17,544 --> 00:22:19,338
Because they thought it was

268
00:22:19,963 --> 00:22:21,048
a prank.

269
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:22,591
Like some social experiment.

270
00:22:23,675 --> 00:22:24,760
We just didn't know
what to do with our money

271
00:22:24,843 --> 00:22:26,094
back then.

272
00:22:38,565 --> 00:22:40,150
But seriously.

273
00:22:51,078 --> 00:22:53,080
I really thought

274
00:22:53,163 --> 00:22:56,083
you wouldn't be able
to make it to my wedding.

275
00:23:07,719 --> 00:23:08,553
You know,

276
00:23:09,096 --> 00:23:13,266
I'm really getting stressed out
because of that GAGO.

277
00:23:13,892 --> 00:23:17,896
I'm so stressed, I need to schedule
a session with my doctor.

278
00:23:18,772 --> 00:23:20,607
Your doctor already went abroad.

279
00:23:21,399 --> 00:23:22,734
When will they be back? No!

280
00:23:22,818 --> 00:23:25,195
Call them and tell them
this is an urgent matter.

281
00:23:25,278 --> 00:23:26,488
Tell them to come home.

282
00:23:27,197 --> 00:23:29,157
Apparently, even your doctor

283
00:23:29,241 --> 00:23:32,244
is now being investigated by GAGO agents.

284
00:23:33,620 --> 00:23:35,163
Son of a…

285
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:37,415
tofu!

286
00:23:38,917 --> 00:23:40,210
And apparently, you're

287
00:23:40,293 --> 00:23:42,003
next on their list to investigate.

288
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:49,427
They won't find anything
in their investigation.

289
00:23:53,223 --> 00:23:57,310
I have solid connections
in different government departments!

290
00:23:57,394 --> 00:23:58,353
Let them try me.

291
00:24:00,939 --> 00:24:02,607
I'm just not going to let

292
00:24:02,691 --> 00:24:05,360
myself be the only one stressed out.

293
00:24:11,032 --> 00:24:13,785
I don't want them to be
the only ones having fun.

294
00:24:25,463 --> 00:24:26,798
La Morte Bianca's Mama Yaya?

295
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:29,509
Your nanny when you trained in Sicily?

296
00:24:38,310 --> 00:24:40,437
<i>Love wears many faces.</i>

297
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:43,315
<i>There are many ways to care</i>

298
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:45,609
<i>and many ways to sacrifice.</i>

299
00:24:45,692 --> 00:24:47,527
<i>But we are always have to choose.</i>

300
00:24:48,111 --> 00:24:49,946
<i>There's always a decision to make.</i>

301
00:24:50,030 --> 00:24:51,740
<i>And until the very end,</i>

302
00:24:51,823 --> 00:24:54,075
<i>I will choose to love</i>
<i>in the only way I know how.</i>

303
00:24:54,743 --> 00:24:57,662
<i>For the person I love most.</i>

304
00:25:11,551 --> 00:25:14,304
MJ? What's the update?

305
00:25:14,387 --> 00:25:16,932
Why is it taking so long
for the door to open?

306
00:25:17,015 --> 00:25:18,725
MJ. MJ!
